      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LIGHTYEAR (1) was out of the money two starts ago then things went amiss last start when he copped a check, broke, and finished a long last over 1660m at Albion Park. Has the benefit of a good draw this time. Facing a tougher assignment but he is up to the challenge. EL JEFE (4) finished third last start, beaten 22 metres at Redcliffe over 1780m. Expecting a very good run. CASUA ART (6) faces the starter for the first time. By Art Major and hails from the Steve Towns stable. Should enjoy a nice smother from this draw and will be looking for a split at some stage. Any push in betting will add to the confidence. MISS ESSVEE (3) is at the track for the first time. By Mcwicked and hails from the Colin Knox stable. Has the benefit of a good draw. Makes plenty of appeal.",
